{"seconds": 108.4, "exit": 0, "final": "After Rb4 f6, White can play Rxd4 and win the queen! So even quiet moves don't help Black. Rb4 is definitely the best move.\n\n**Coaching Note (for the player):**\n\nAfter your opponent plays Ng4, the knight becomes a defender and a target. Look for **Rb4** - it attacks Black's queen and forces it into a difficult position. Every escape square leads to losing material: if the queen captures (Qxb4), you continue with Rxf7 and dominate. The key is recognizing when a defender can be overloaded with attacks. This is a **fork** or **double attack** - your rook pressures both the queen and the follow-up tactics on the kingside.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Rb4\", \"line\": [\"Rb4\", \"Qxb4\", \"Rxf7\", \"Qe1+\", \"Qxe1\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"deflection\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "2kr3r/ppp2ppp/8/1P6/3q2n1/P2Pp3/1RP1B2P/Q4RK1 w - - 2 21"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "2kr3r/ppp2ppp/8/1P6/3q2n1/P2Pp3/1RP1B2P/Q4RK1 w - - 2 21"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "2kr3r/ppp2ppp/8/1P6/3q2n1/P2Pp3/1RP1B2P/Q4RK1 w - - 2 21", "square": "d4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "2kr3r/ppp2ppp/8/1P6/3q2n1/P2Pp3/1RP1B2P/Q4RK1 w - - 2 21", "square": "g4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "2kr3r/ppp2ppp/8/1P6/3q2n1/P2Pp3/1RP1B2P/Q4RK1 w - - 2 21", "square": "a1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "2kr3r/ppp2ppp/8/1P6/3q2n1/P2Pp3/1RP1B2P/Q4RK1 w - - 2 21", "square": "f1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "2kr3r/ppp2ppp/8/1P6/3q2n1/P2Pp3/1RP1B2P/Q4RK1 w - - 2 21"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2kr3r/ppp2ppp/8/1P6/3q2n1/P2Pp3/1RP1B2P/Q4RK1 w - - 2 21", "move": "Rb4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2kr3r/ppp2ppp/8/1P6/3q2n1/P2Pp3/1RP1B2P/Q4RK1 w - - 2 21", "move": "Rxf7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspe